hnology","HSVR":"House Committee on Veterans' Affairs","HSWM":"House Committee on Ways and Means","JCSE":"Commission on Security and Cooperation in Europe","JSEC":"Joint Economic Committee","JSLC":"Joint Committee of Congress on the Library","JSPR":"Joint Committee on Printing","JSTX":"Joint Committee on Taxation","SCNC":"United States Senate Caucus on International Narcotics Control","SLET":"Senate Select Committee on Ethics","SLIA":"Senate Committee on Indian Affairs","SLIN":"Senate Select Committee on Intelligence","SPAG":"Senate Special Committee on Aging","SSAF":"Senate Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry","SSAP":"Senate Committee on Appropriations","SSAS":"Senate Committee on Armed Services","SSBK":"Senate Committee on Banking, Housing, and Urban Affairs","SSBU":"Senate Committee on the Budget","SSCM":"Senate Committee on Commerce, Science, and Transportation","SSEG":"Senate Committee on Energy and Natural Resources","SSEV":"Senate Committee on Environment and Public Works","SSFI":"Senate Committee on Finance","SSFR":"Senate Committee on Foreign Relations","SSGA":"Senate Committee on Homeland Security and Governmental Affairs","SSHR":"Senate Committee on Health, Education, Labor, and Pensions","SSJU":"Senate Committee on the Judiciary","SSRA":"Senate Committee on Rules and Administration","SSSB":"Senate Committee on Small Business and Entrepreneurship","SSVA":"Senate Committee on Veterans' Affairs","HSZS":"House Select Committee on the Strategic Competition Between the United States and the Chinese Communist Party","HSQJ":"House Select Subcommittee to Investigate the Remaining Questions Surrounding January 6, 2021"},"mapping":{"_purpose":"Each committee's policy areas expressed as industries, for the committee-overlap check. Industries are ranges of SEC Standard Industrial Classification (SIC) codes. Conservative by design: a committee is mapped only to industries named in its written jurisdiction, and broad or indirect jurisdiction (tax, appropriations, antitrust) is left out. Published with the data so the result can be checked.","status":"reviewed 2026-10-04 against the jurisdiction texts below","sources":{"house":"Rules of the House of Representatives, 119th Congress, Rule X clause 1: https://rules.house.gov/sites/evo-subsites/rules.house.gov/files/documents/houserules119thupdated.pdf","senate":"Standing Rules of the Senate, Rule XXV paragraph 1 (S. Doc. 113-18): https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CDOC-113sdoc18/pdf/CDOC-113sdoc18.pdf","subcommittees":"Subcommittee names from unitedstates/congress-legislators committees-current.json"},"funds":{"why":"Exchange-traded trusts that SEC files under a SIC code (bitcoin, gold, silver, platinum). They hold a commodity, not a company, so they are left out like other funds.","sic":[[6221,6221]]},"industries":{"defense":{"label":"Defense and aerospace","sic":[[3480,3489],[3720,3729],[3730,3732],[3760,3769],[3795,3795],[3812,3812]]},"fossil_fuels":{"label":"Oil, gas, coal and pipelines","sic":[[1200,1299],[1300,1399],[2900,2999],[4610,4619],[4920,4925]]},"utilities":{"label":"Electric and gas utilities","sic":[[4900,4919],[4926,4991]]},"mining":{"label":"Metal and mineral mining","sic":[[1000,1099],[1400,1499]]},"finance":{"label":"Banks, insurance, brokers and real estate","sic":[[6000,6799]]},"housing":{"label":"Homebuilders","sic":[[1520,1531]]},"health":{"label":"Drugs, medical devices, pharmacies, health care and insurers","sic":[[2833,2836],[3841,3845],[5122,5122],[5912,5912],[6324,6324],[8000,8099]]},"telecom":{"label":"Telecommunications and media","sic":[[4800,4899]]},"tech":{"label":"Computers, semiconductors, software and internet","sic":[[3570,3579],[3660,3679],[7370,7379]]},"autos":{"label":"Cars, trucks and parts","sic":[[3711,3716]]},"transport":{"label":"Airlines, rail, trucking and shipping","sic":[[3743,3743],[4000,4599],[4700,4799]]},"agriculture":{"label":"Farming, meat, dairy, grain, sugar and farm inputs","sic":[[100,999],[2010,2029],[2040,2048],[2060,2063],[2070,2079],[2870,2879],[3523,3523],[5150,5159]]},"education":{"label":"Education services","sic":[[8200,8299]]}},"committees":{"HSAG":{"industries":["agriculture"],"why":"Agriculture generally, commodity prices, livestock and meat inspection, dairy, agricultural chemistry. Packaged food and drinks are left out: the text covers farm products, not food manufacturing. Commodity exchanges (CFTC) are left out: they are markets, not a sector.","source":"House Rule X, clause 1(a)"},"SSAF":{"industries":["agriculture"],"why":"Agricultural production and commodities, livestock and meat inspection, pests and pesticides, farm credit.","source":"Senate Rule XXV, paragraph 1(a)"},"HSAS":{"industries":["defense"],"why":"The Department of Defense, the common defense, and military research and development.","source":"House Rule X, clause 1(c)"},"SSAS":{"industries":["defense"],"why":"The Department of Defense, weapons systems and military research and development.","source":"Senate Rule XXV, paragraph 1(c)"},"HSBA":{"industries":["finance","housing"],"why":"Banks and banking, insurance generally, securities and exchanges, public and private housing.","source":"House Rule X, clause 1(h)"},"SSBK":{"industries":["finance","housing"],"why":"Banks and financial institutions, public and private housing. Securities and insurance sit with its Securities, Insurance, and Investment subcommittee (SEC).","source":"Senate Rule XXV, paragraph 1(d)"},"HSIF":{"industries":["fossil_fuels","utilities","health","telecom","tech","autos"],"why":"Energy resources including all fossil fuels, power generation and transmission, health and public health, communications, interstate commerce and consumer protection (subcommittees on Communications and Technology, and Commerce, Manufacturing, and Trade). Automobile safety sits here: Rule X excludes it from Transportation.","source":"House Rule X, clause 1(f)"},"HSII":{"industries":["fossil_fuels","mining"],"why":"Mining interests generally, mineral resources and petroleum on public lands.","source":"House Rule X, clause 1(m)"},"SSEG":{"industries":["fossil_fuels","utilities","mining"],"why":"Coal, oil and gas production, energy regulation, hydroelectric power, mining and mineral lands.","source":"Senate Rule XXV, paragraph 1(g)"},"SSEV":{"industries":["utilities"],"why":"Air pollution and civilian nuclear regulation, which govern power plants. Highways and public works are left out: they are spending, not a sector.","source":"Senate Rule XXV, paragraph 1(h)"},"HSPW":{"industries":["transport"],"why":"Civil aviation, railroads, water transportation, trucking and roads. Automobile safety is excluded by the rule.","source":"House Rule X, clause 1(r)"},"SSCM":{"industries":["transport","telecom","tech","autos"],"why":"Communications, common carriers (rail, trucks, aviation), highway safety, consumer products, and technology policy (subcommittee on Consumer Protection, Technology, and Data Privacy).","source":"Senate Rule XXV, paragraph 1(f)"},"HSWM":{"industries":["health"],"why":"Health care funded by payroll deductions (Medicare), through its Health subcommittee. Tax and trade touch every industry and are left out.","source":"House Rule X, clause 1(t)"},"SSFI":{"industries":["health"],"why":"Health programs under the Social Security Act (Medicare and Medicaid). Tax and trade touch every industry and are left out.","source":"Senate Rule XXV, paragraph 1(i)"},"SSHR":{"industries":["health","education"],"why":"Public health, biomedical research, education and student loans.","source":"Senate Rule XXV, paragraph 1(l)"},"HSED":{"industries":["education"],"why":"Education generally and the Department of Education.","source":"House Rule X, clause 1(e)"},"HSSY":{"industries":[],"why":"Research funding (NASA, NSF, energy research). It funds research rather than regulating a sector."},"HSHM":{"industries":[],"why":"Homeland security; contracting touches many industries without a clear sector."},"SSGA":{"industries":